  "observations": [
    "Sortformer loads and runs in the pinned v0.2.2 CLI. Not a negative result.",
    "The CLI path never holds capture by construction: it reads a finished .wav from disk and exits. Spike 3's capture invariant is therefore not exercised here \u2014 it is a question for the later in-process bind (spec/50 \u00a73), where Sortformer must load as a separate model from the STT model (D8 is per-model, so Parakeet + Sortformer is two loads and is allowed).",
    "Sortformer has no expected-speakers input. The current path's Auto/2/3/4 clustering hint (speaker.meeting.num_speakers) has no analog: the model is a fixed 4-slot arrival-order diarizer. On this fixture that costs nothing (both agree on 2), but a `sortformer` diarizer option would silently ignore an existing config key.",
    "The coverage gap is the one behavioural difference that could reach users: meeting.AttributeTranscript maps transcript segments onto the timeline, and 15.1 s of audio that currently falls inside a coarse sherpa span would fall into a Sortformer inter-span gap. Whether that yields unlabelled turns depends on AttributeTranscript's overlap/nearest rule and was not measured in this spike.",
    "Sortformer labels are arrival-order only, with no cross-recording identity \u2014 same as the current path's speaker-N, so enrollment/naming remains unaffected.",
    "Single fixture, single meeting, 2 speakers, one 4.8 s interjection. This is one data point and it does not exercise the 3-4 speaker or overlapped-speech regimes where the current path's Auto over-split is a known failure."
  ]
}
